    "turn_text": "From 12 News, this is Newsmakers. It's been a rollercoaster summer for Democrats. President Biden quit the presidential race after intense pressure from other senior leaders. Now, Vice President Kamala Harris is riding a wave of momentum as she seeks to overtake former President Donald Trump in the polls. Newly elected Congressman Gabe Amo has had a front-row seat for it all, even joining Biden in Las Vegas for what turned out to be his last campaign stop. Where do Democrats go from here? We'll ask our guest this week on Newsmakers Rhode Island Congressman Gabe Ommo. Welcome to Newsmakers. I'm Tim White, alongside 12 news politics editor Ted Nisi, and we welcome our guest. Congressman Gabe Amma, welcome back to the program. It's good to have you. Thanks for having me. So we have a lot to talk about, Congressman, but we have to start with Trump's comments, former President Donald Trump's comments during a session with the National Association of Black Journalists. It's made a lot of news in recent days, especially his comments on Vice President Kamala Harris' race. Let's take a listen.",
