    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "The first reaction was what year are we living in? This is 2024. We should be able to talk about issues of identity without the weird cynicism and frankly dog whistling that you have a former President Trump putting forward. It is clear as she describes herself, the vice president is black and of South Asian heritage Indian. That is a fact. I think this is another attempt to be backwards looking and frankly bizarre. Think about this. Remember the whole birth certificate, birtherism with former President Obama. This is a dog whistle to certain folks who want to look at race as a scary thing. We are a diverse country. I am honored to be someone who brings a perspective from my background that is a little bit different than others here in Rhode Island. So I think when you look at President Trump, former President Trump, Think about his intentions. His intentions are to fear monger, to obscure. And really, this",
