  {
    "episode_id": 91062,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91062.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "I did want to ask a zoom out question on this, because you just ran for office last year, as you just alluded to. You're the first black person to ever represent Rhode Island in Congress. And when you were campaigning, you were in a line which I heard you used frequently, which is, I'm not running to make history. I'm running to make a difference. And it was clear that, well, you didn't shy away from people mentioning that you would make history in terms of your identity. You didn't feel it was something you wanted to be talking about all the time. Just how did you, because it is, it's who you are. How did you think about that? That makes sense like you as a person versus you as a candidate.",
