    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think we have to celebrate the success that both the president and vice president were involved in. I'm reading so many accounts of this. Really harrowing stuff. But of course, we can't be satisfied with Putin's frankly dictatorial leadership there and wanting to push forward his autocratic dreams in Ukraine and empowering these folks is always a risk. But deal making is part of the job. You've got to take the bad with the good. And I am grateful that we have Evan Gurskovich back. I'm grateful that we have Paul Whelan back, the other journalist who was captured. I know I used that hashtag and tried to promote the cause because it is about some of us all vital to us, journalism. and ensuring that people can communicate freely about the wrongs and the rights in this world. And that's what he symbolized in lots of ways. And beyond that, what I do think we need to continue to be mindful of is the alliances that brought us here. And this is something that Foreign President Trump doesn't really believe in. Remember, Germany and Slovenia, both key parts of making this deal. And so a united world with strong global alliances will overcome Putin and his negative and dark vision for the world. And I'm grateful that we have our Americans back home.",
