    "turn_text": "been mixed. I think we can be very clear that some people are doing very well in our economy. So you look at, especially because of the concentration of wealth from the Trump tax cuts, you have real inequities. But at the same time, remember where we were at the beginning of the COVID-19 crisis. Remember where we were when President Biden and Vice President Harris took office. We're on the brink of a full on economic collapse. And because of their work, we've pulled out, but not everybody's benefited. I'm not going to sugarcoat it. And I would say this slowdown that we saw in today's job report may inspire some action by the Fed. Should they lower the rate? You know, I try not to get into the politics of it, but it seems prudent to do so. And I know it's because it's a couple months before an election. So I don't want them to be mired in the politics, but it seems like it will ease a burden on the economy. And we know that it's just been really expensive to do things. We're feeling it here in Rhode Island. I talk to people every day, costs, are issue one, two or three for many road islanders when I see them in the grocery store. And I know that we need to do more. And so I think the vice president will have a very candid conversation about what we need to do. We certainly need to go after price gouging. We certainly need to have a fair tax code. And we also need to make sure that some of the costs that we're incurring on housing on energy prices are things that we are responsive to with the swiftness that they deserve.",
